# A toy .acme netlist read by the overlay's private format reader.
#
# Two house-rule violations are seeded, one per overlay rule:
#   X1 uses an X-prefixed ref-des        -> acme/no-experimental-refdes (a Go rule)
#   X1 sits on VCC, which carries U1's
#   declared power pin                   -> acme/experimental-on-power-net (a datalog rule)
#
# `pin` lines declare PART-TYPE pins, which is what the engine's pin relations project from. A
# net connection alone says a pin is wired; only a pin declaration says the pin exists, what it
# is called, and what type it is.
component R1 resistor 10k
component C1 cap 100n
component U1 mcu
component X1 widget

pin U1 1 VDD power_in
pin U1 2 GPIO0 output
pin U1 8 VSS power_in
pin X1 1 IO inout
pin X1 3 GND power_in

net VCC R1.1 C1.1 U1.1 X1.2
net GND R1.2 C1.2 U1.8 X1.3
net SIG U1.2 X1.1
